<title>MOROCCO: French groups to build Moroccan nuclear centre.</title>
<headline>French groups to build Moroccan nuclear centre.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two French groups Technicatome and SPIE-Batignolles have signed a contract to build Morocco's first nuclear centre in collaboration with the French atomic energy commission, the Moroccan news agency MAP reported.</p>
<p>It said the contract was signed on Thursday night after Moroccan Finance Minister Mohamed Kabbaj and French Foreign Trade Minister Yves Galland signed a 520 million francs ($97.9 million) loan accord to finance the centre and the purchase of nine railway engines.</p>
<p>The plant, on 25 hectares (62.5 acres), will be located in Maamora about 15 kms (nine miles) from Rabat and will have a two megawatt American research reactor and technically advanced laboratories.</p>
